    "answer": {
      "short": "$21.8^\\circ$",
      "worked": "Since $XYZW$ is a rectangle, Pythagoras gives\n$$\\begin{align*}XZ^2&=XY^2+YZ^2\\\\XZ^2&=4^2+3^2\\\\XZ&=5\\,\\mathrm{cm}.\\end{align*}$$\nThe angle of elevation is $\\theta=\\angle SXZ$, between $XS$ and its horizontal projection $XZ$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{ZS}{XZ}\\\\\\tan\\theta&=\\frac{2}{5}\\\\\\theta&\\approx21.8^\\circ.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
